WEBVTT

00:00:03.259 --> 00:00:11.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning all, you alright? Let's get cracking, Monday 25th. Quick stand-up, just run the board and no essays if we can help it.</v>

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:21.309
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Morning. Sorry, traffic on the ring road was horrendous, proper standstill by the slip, so if I sound a bit grumpy that's why.</v>

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:29.190
<v David Whitfield>You and everyone else. There is a birthday cake in the office though, so, you know, morale's recovered a bit.</v>

00:00:31.649 --> 00:00:39.000
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah and whose new car is that in the car park? The grey one. Looks way too clean for this place.</v>

00:00:41.409 --> 00:00:45.259
<v Jamie Brennan>Won't be mine, mine still sounds like a bag of bolts.</v>

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:50.679
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, focus, cake and cars later. Any carry-overs, completions, blockers?</v>

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:59.469
<v Olumide Adeyemi>From me, I tested the new line yesterday and it's all fine now, so that's done, nothing else needed there.</v>

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:06.840
<v David Whitfield>I signed off the inspection on the Atlas on Tuesday, so that's closed out as well.</v>

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:12.989
<v Jamie Brennan>And I already swapped the filter on the stacker yesterday, before anyone asks, so that's done.</v>

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:30.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. I've just got an observation from the floor: I saw the pressure on the pick and place on two dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own. Just keeping an eye on it, not a job for today unless it repeats.</v>

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:38.890
<v Fiona Doyle>Blocker from planning side, still waiting on parts for the dryer, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:40.019 --> 00:01:48.769
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah and on access, can't get to the stacker until production gives us a window. So that's still sat there, not ignored, just no slot.</v>

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:57.430
<v David Whitfield>Also, just so nobody plans around it, the shutdown on the MV01 is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:01:59.379 --> 00:02:02.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, noted, MV01 cancelled. Fine. David, anything else from mechanical?</v>

00:02:04.519 --> 00:02:12.219
<v David Whitfield>Nothing live from me apart from the usual noises and leaks, really. Plant's a bit scruffy after weekend but no fresh drama.</v>

00:02:14.419 --> 00:02:15.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, stores?</v>

00:02:16.699 --> 00:02:23.000
<v Jamie Brennan>Mostly receipts this morning. Bit thin on bearings, but manageable. I can look at paperwork bits if needed.</v>

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:35.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Actually, on paperwork, we need to update the risk assessment for work on the hot bearing. Jamie, can you take that and get it sorted for next Tuesday? Top priority please.</v>

00:02:36.009 --> 00:02:45.460
<v Jamie Brennan>Uh, not really the best person for that one, Sarah. I can pull documents but I shouldn't be owning the risk assessment for the hot bearing itself.</v>

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:54.830
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, fair. Olu, can you pick that up instead and update the risk assessment for work on the hot bearing, next Tuesday, top priority please?</v>

00:02:55.689 --> 00:03:07.240
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, alright, I'll do it. I'll update the risk assessment for work on the hot bearing and have that done for next Tuesday. If Jamie sends me the latest revision it'll be quicker.</v>

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.370
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll send you the current pack straight after this.</v>

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, that's agreed. Aisha, process side?</v>

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:23.199
<v Aisha Begum>Morning. Nothing huge. The alarm box purchase order still hasn't shown up in the system, which is getting a bit silly.</v>

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:36.069
<v Aisha Begum>I was going to chase the purchase order for the alarm box, but I've got the solvent balance and the wash trials stacked up this morning, so I'm not going to get near it.</v>

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:43.349
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I can grab that. I'll chase the purchase order for the alarm box by 11am, no problem.</v>

00:03:44.699 --> 00:03:45.900
<v Aisha Begum>Perfect, cheers.</v>

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:50.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one. Mide's got that by 11am.</v>

00:03:52.289 --> 00:04:01.039
<v Fiona Doyle>On planning, before we get buried, the FLTs still need a proper slot with production. Normal priority, nothing dramatic, but it does need booking in.</v>

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:09.270
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll schedule downtime for the FLTs with production. Normal priority, I'll get it lined up when they're in this morning.</v>

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks Doyler.</v>

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:19.870
<v Fiona Doyle>And I'll send the shift handover report round tomorrow. I was going to do it Friday and then, well, Friday happened.</v>

00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:23.970
<v David Whitfield>Friday happened to all of us, to be fair.</v>

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:34.829
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Fiona, separate one: I need you to investigate the pressure drop on the IM1 hydraulic unit today. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:36.800
<v Fiona Doyle>Me, yeah?</v>

00:04:38.629 --> 00:04:44.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, you. Investigate the pressure drop on the IM1 hydraulic unit today. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:04:45.629 --> 00:04:51.230
<v Fiona Doyle>Alright, understood. I'll investigate the pressure drop on the IM1 hydraulic unit today, straight after this.</v>

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:56.670
<v David Whitfield>If you want a second pair of eyes later, shout.</v>

00:04:57.089 --> 00:04:58.290
<v Fiona Doyle>Might do, cheers.</v>

00:04:59.689 --> 00:05:10.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, on the stacker, separate from the access issue, can you go to the hydraulics lot to pick up the replacement parts for the stacker after lunch? Top priority please.</v>

00:05:11.319 --> 00:05:19.019
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I can do that. I'll go to the hydraulics lot to pick up the replacement parts for the stacker after lunch.</v>

00:05:21.029 --> 00:05:22.230
<v Sarah Okafor>Good man.</v>

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:30.430
<v Marcus Hale>Just to be clear, that's pick up the parts after lunch. Fitting's still blocked till production gives us a window.</v>

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:36.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, exactly. Collection today, work window later when they let us in.</v>

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.740
<v Marcus Hale>Sound.</v>

00:05:40.509 --> 00:05:47.160
<v Marcus Hale>While we're on it, the door switch on two's still a bit suspect. Not failed-failed, but it's not right.</v>

00:05:48.839 --> 00:05:52.339
<v David Whitfield>Is that the one that keeps giving the ghost open?</v>

00:05:54.689 --> 00:05:59.589
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, that one. Fairly important before it turns into a nuisance stop every hour.</v>

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:08.250
<v Marcus Hale>I'll order spare parts for the door switch on two. Fairly important, so I'd rather get ahead of it.</v>

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:15.750
<v Jamie Brennan>If you send me the part number I'll make sure stores doesn't bin the request in the usual black hole.</v>

00:06:16.089 --> 00:06:18.889
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, Marc's handwriting department will try its best.</v>

00:06:19.569 --> 00:06:25.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, that's covered. David, anything supporting on IM1 or hot bearing, other than what we've said?</v>

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:37.800
<v David Whitfield>Not as an owned job, no. I can back Fiona up on the IM1 hydraulic unit if needed, and Olu on the hot bearing paperwork if he wants a sanity check.</v>

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:45.860
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, maybe later just sanity check the wording, because if I write 'hot' too many times HSE will have a fit.</v>

00:06:47.279 --> 00:06:49.730
<v David Whitfield>Write 'thermally enthusiastic bearing', sounds more expensive.</v>

00:06:51.829 --> 00:06:54.980
<v Aisha Begum>Put that in a risk assessment, see what happens.</v>

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:59.839
<v Sarah Okafor>Please don't. Right, anything else live that actually needs agreeing today?</v>

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:05.680
<v Jamie Brennan>No new actions from stores. I'll just support on docs and receipts.</v>

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:12.410
<v Aisha Begum>Nothing else from process. Main thing was the alarm box PO and Mide's got that.</v>

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:26.230
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep. Just repeating back so I don't forget: I've got update the risk assessment for work on the hot bearing for next Tuesday, top priority please, and I'll chase the purchase order for the alarm box by 11am.</v>

00:07:28.319 --> 00:07:29.519
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct.</v>

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:45.050
<v Fiona Doyle>And I've got schedule downtime for the FLTs with production, normal priority, plus I'll send the shift handover report round tomorrow, and investigate the pressure drop on the IM1 hydraulic unit today, that one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:47.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Spot on.</v>

00:07:48.230 --> 00:08:00.480
<v Marcus Hale>And me: I'll go to the hydraulics lot to pick up the replacement parts for the stacker after lunch, top priority please, and I'll order spare parts for the door switch on two, fairly important.</v>

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's the lot.</v>

00:08:03.879 --> 00:08:07.379
<v David Whitfield>No one wants me to do anything, which is suspicious.</v>

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:10.600
<v Sarah Okafor>Enjoy it while it lasts.</v>

00:08:11.149 --> 00:08:13.949
<v Jamie Brennan>He can cut the cake, that's his task.</v>

00:08:15.779 --> 00:08:18.230
<v David Whitfield>Finally, a role worthy of my talents.</v>

00:08:19.509 --> 00:08:31.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we descend completely: watch the pick and place on two, but no action unless it drops again. Dryer remains blocked on parts. MV01 shutdown cancelled. Stacker access still waiting on production window.</v>

00:08:33.559 --> 00:08:38.460
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll note those in the planner comments so nobody turns them into phantom jobs.</v>

00:08:39.669 --> 00:08:41.419
<v Sarah Okafor>Perfect. Anything urgent anyone's missed?</v>

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:44.049
<v Aisha Begum>Nope.</v>

00:08:45.759 --> 00:08:46.960
<v Olumide Adeyemi>All good.</v>

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.059
<v Marcus Hale>Fine by me.</v>

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.340
<v David Whitfield>Just the cake, still urgent.</v>

00:08:54.169 --> 00:08:58.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Meeting over. Go on then, five minutes for cake and then back out.</v>
